we just got a huge flurry of iphone 14  pro leaks over the weekend that helped  confirm a lot of the leaks and rumors  that we just weren't sure about until  this point including reports that the  design is now finalized and we shouldn't  see any more changes after this point  which is great news and now before i get  into the very interesting details about  which ports the iphone 14 pro is most  likely to come with let's first get into  what everyone's been talking about over  this weekend and that's the brand new  hole punch cutout display  about a month and a half ago we started  to see confirmation for the original  display panel leak from shrimp apple pro  which showed two cutouts replacing the  current face id notch now initially the  idea was that the extra hole on the side  would be invisible with part of the face  id system shining through it under the  display leaving a nice pill-shaped  cutout perfectly centered in the middle  but that ended up getting debunked with  some rumor confirmation and that  confirmation actually came from ross  young who was a display analyst with a  100 track record in terms of apple leaks  including perfectly predicting the  display size of the ipad mini 6 as well  as mini led and pro motion coming to the  new macbook pros on january 12th he said  that this display panel leak was real  and that the extra hole punch would  remain visible with a new unique  two-hole concept and even though it  looks a bit weird the idea is that it  would allow the iphone to continue to  look completely different from any other  design out there which is very important  to apple but what ended up happening was  that everyone on the internet started to  create renders of this new design with  hole punch cutouts that were pretty  small and sleek but over this weekend we  got a major leak from a weibo source  that completely spoiled the party a  display schematic was leaked by a  chinese source showing a much larger  dual cutout than everybody expected but  the most important part is that it  actually kind of looks like it could be  an official leaked schematic and even  better it was confirmed by multiple  sources including john prosser who said  he was able to independently confirm  that this schematic is legitimate and  that this was likely the size of the  cutouts now the weird thing is that the  size doesn't really match the original  display panel leak from shrimp apple pro  who by the way has been saying that his  panel leak was from the back side  so it should actually be flipped when on  the iphone matching the cutout  orientation of this new schematic leak  but the part that doesn't really match  up is the size since the cutouts on the  original display panel leak seemed to be  quite a bit smaller than the ones on the  new schematic and thankfully shrimp  apple pro sent out a newsletter on  sunday to explain the entire situation  with the size difference apparently back  in august he said that the cutouts will  be weirdly big basically confirming  these recent schematic leaks that look  big and then to explain the difference  in the sizes shrimp believes that this  new schematic is for the 6.1 inch iphone  14 pro model while his original panel  leak was for the larger 6.7 inch model  which is why the cutouts look smaller  against the larger display so it looks  like apple is going to be taking the  simple route of tweaking the face id  sensor system then cutting holes around  it and then removing the black paint of  the current notch that we have which  would lead to a design that looks like  this which is exactly what i showed you  guys in a video i made a month and a  half ago with this really sloppy  photoshop sketch and while a lot of you  guys online aren't happy with the news  of the cutouts being larger than  expected i personally think it's gonna  look great especially on the max model  which i prefer  and it's gonna put the notch to shane  and speaking of the notch shrimp  confirmed that the new cutout design is  only for the pro models while the  regular 14 and 14 max models will  continue to come with the same old notch  that we currently have on the 13 models  and this right here was actually an old  leak from ross young which he recently  confirmed once again over the weekend  but the most important confirmation that  he gave us was that next year all four  of the iphone 15 models will come with  this new dual hull design hopefully with  smaller holes than we saw in this new  schematic but nevertheless this means  that the notch will finally be going  away for good on the iphone so if you're  planning on skipping the iphone 14 this  year next year is going to be awesome  for the lower end iphone 15 models now  that the notch is going to be gone and  as far as 120 hertz pro motion  technology ross young confirmed that for  the iphone 15 lineup it's still only  gonna be on the pro models and not any  of the lower end models so i would still  recommend going for the pro models right  now because 120 hertz has been my  favorite feature so far with the 13 pro  max now on top of all of these display  and design leaks we also got some  important leaks concerning the general  features and the specs for example we  got a report from taiwan's economic  daily news that the iphone 14 lineup  should have better battery life thanks  to a new 5g chip which will be produced  using tsmc's new six nanometer process  which is more efficient but on top of  that it also means that we should get  less overheating while using 5g which  has been causing some problems with the  current iphones while running high  performance tasks on 5g like gaming but  the part that i'm really looking forward  to is the addition of wi-fi 6e with the  new 6 gigahertz band which will be a  much bigger deal than the current wi-fi  6 which didn't really seem to change  much at all going further we got some  reports from a korean blogger who claims  that the iphone 14 pro will come with 8  gigabytes of ram this year and this is  after an analyst jeff poo said that we  should be getting eight gigs so i'm  pretty confident that this is gonna  happen and now another leaked feature  that we finally got some more clarity on  is under display touch id which has been  leaked for many years already and as you  guys may know i've been saying that ever  since apple allowed face id to work with  masks i honestly don't think that apple  will ever need under display touch id  and it looks like all of the leaks are  pointing to this happening first of all  shrimp apple pro confirmed that touch id  will not be coming on the iphone 14  which is something he's been saying ever  since august and even more recently  leaks apple pro has reported to eyedrop  news that apple is no longer working on  under display touch id for the iphone  which basically means that they're  completely scrapping this idea and in my  opinion this makes sense because face id  is completely exclusive to apple there's  literally nothing out there that's like  it while under display fingerprint  scanners are everywhere so i think that  apple is going to stick with face id for  many many years maybe even decades as  they improve on the technology by adding  even more layers of security now finally  the last thing i want to talk about is  the port situation and as you guys may  know i made a video a couple months back  discussing why i think it makes sense  for the iphone 14 pro to come with usbc  instead of lightning and within that  video i made the very important point  that when apple revealed lightning they  said that it would be the port that  they'd use for the next decade and guess  what that was 10 years ago in 2012. so  this basically confirms that either this  year or next year apple will for sure be  ditching lightning on the iphone and i  personally think it's going to be this  year because they might as well do it  alongside this new fold redesign  especially since we're expected to get a  48 megapixel camera on the pro models  for shooting 8k video so we're gonna  need the faster transfer speeds but  since making that video apple has  apparently discontinued the iphone  lightning dock which could be a major  hint that points to them beginning to  ditch lightning completely and even  though the last thing minchiko said  about usbc on the iphone was that apple  would be sticking to lightning for the  foreseeable future that was actually  back in march of last year so maybe  things have changed and that is what i'm  personally hoping for but no matter what  happens with the port the important  thing is that the dual cutout face id  display design is now confirmed to be  coming and finalized and it's gonna help  the iphone look a lot better than before  so hopefully you guys enjoyed this video  and if you did click that circle above  to subscribe for more videos like this  one and definitely check out some of  those videos right there including the  new samsung s22 ultra comparisons thanks  for watching and we'll see you in the  next video  [Music]
 

